## 2. Four-tier verdict

> **SPOT-CHECK ✅** (honest caveat: only ~20 % of the paper's quantitative content is even *in-principle* reproducible from the paper text; that sliver reproduces cleanly).

- **REPLICATED** — no. Full reproduction of Figs 7–14, 17, 18 (RHR survival curves, LDA/HDA decomposition, weekly-fractionation P+ gains, secondary-cancer-risk model) is **physically impossible from the paper text alone**: the formulae and fitted parameters live in the author's prior closed/figure-embedded publications (refs 7, 9, 10, 15).
- **PARTIAL** — no. "Partial" would require reproducing a non-trivial fraction of the quantitative figures; the paper's figures are nearly all schematic re-plots of curves whose parameters are not in this paper.
- **SPOT-CHECK ✅** — yes. *Every explicit closed-form numerical claim the paper makes from its own text* reproduces to ≥3 significant figures (Eq. 1 + 4 Gumbel statistics + Fig. 12 caption microdosimetry arithmetic + Fig. 5/6 narrative identities).
- **NO-GO** — no. Nothing in the paper's own closed-form math is contradicted; internal consistency holds (with one minor paper-side rounding glitch, see C1 below).

